  "hidden_pattern": "The ubiquitous 4.7 kOhm pull-up is a Standard-mode (100 kHz) component. At 3.3 V it limits Cb to 251 pF in Standard mode, 75 pF in Fast mode, and 30 pF in Fast-mode Plus. Fast mode at 400 pF and 3.3 V has an empty window (Rp_min > Rp_max) with the 3 mA sink specified for Standard/Fast mode. Fast-mode Plus is feasible at 550 pF only because its sink current is 20 mA; reusing the 3 mA number manufactures a false impossibility. The 0.8473 in Rp(max) is ln(7/3), not a fitted constant.",
